course: dictionary
lesson: 10500
title: Tweezers: a tool word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A tool word names something you use to do a job. Tweezers is a tool word. Read this: «Ask an adult to take out a splinter with clean tweezers, because a splinter left in can get infected.» The job is taking out a splinter, so tweezers must be the thing that does the pulling.
explain: Look at the ending. «Tweezers» ends in s, and it is usually plural, so we say a pair of tweezers, not one tweezers. Scissors and glasses work the same way. The singular tweezer can come before another noun, but you will mostly meet the plural.
explain: Context also tells you how tweezers work. «Tongs and tweezers are levers pressed in the middle» means you squeeze the middle to close the arms. They give less force but more control, so they suit careful work, like picking up a tiny seed.
fact: Tweezers are a small tool with two thin metal arms that you squeeze together.
fact: Tweezers are used to pick up or pull out tiny things, such as a splinter.
fact: Tweezers are usually plural, so say a pair of tweezers.
fact: Scientists use tweezers to pick up small things like seeds or insects without crushing them.
fact: Use clean tweezers, and let an adult remove a splinter or a tick; a deep splinter may need a doctor.
exercise: «Ask an adult to take out a splinter with clean tweezers.» What are tweezers used for? | *Picking up or pulling out tiny things | Carrying hot water | Cutting long grass | Pressing a cut shut
exercise: Which phrase names the tool correctly? | *a pair of tweezers | three tweezer | one tweezers | two tweezer
exercise: «After walking in long grass, check your skin for ticks; if you find one, an adult removes it with fine tweezers.» What does an adult use to remove a tick? | A hot bath | A big spoon | A paint brush | *Fine tweezers
test: «Tongs and tweezers are levers pressed in the middle.» Why do tweezers suit careful work? | They only work on wood | They give more force, so they crush small things | They need no hands to use | *They give less force but more control
test: Why should the tweezers be clean before a splinter is taken out? | So they are lighter | So they look shiny | So they can be used for cooking | *So the splinter does not get infected
exam: Which sentence describes tweezers correctly? | Tweezers are a type of cloth | Tweezers are a loud kind of bird | *Tweezers are a small tool with two thin metal arms | Tweezers are a big bowl for water
